(Growth can move a buffer, so a byte read or write that held the buffer
 across a call growing it would touch released memory. The index and the
 value are worked out first, then the buffer is read or written as it is.)
To 'grow' with a buffer called data.
    For each number from 1 to 3000, append "abcdefgh" to data.
    Return a number, 2.

a buffer called hold is "AB".
a number called b is byte {'grow' of hold} of hold.
Print "byte: {b}, size: {hold's size}".
a buffer called spot is "AB".
Set byte 1 of spot to 'grow' of spot.
Print "first byte: {byte 1 of spot}, size: {spot's size}".
